       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily (15 g/day) is a toxic dose. It could cause severe liver injury or liver failure, and I can't find a clinical scenario where it would be appropriate. You also haven't given a rationale.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a safe dose.** I can enter up to 1000 mg PO every 6\u20138 hours, with a maximum of 4 g/day (or less, depending on your institution's limits).\n- **Call pharmacy.** If you're treating a specific situation, such as an overdose or an unusual protocol, a pharmacist or toxicology can help with the right regimen. Treating an acetaminophen overdose usually means N-acetylcysteine, not more acetaminophen.\n- **Check the source.** If the dose came from a handwritten note, a template, or a verbal order, it may be a transcription error.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
